  {
    q: 'What is the difference between FCL and LCL for China to Ireland?',
    a: 'FCL is priced per container (northern-range benchmark 20ft $1,200–$4,800, 40ft $1,600–$6,800; Dublin/Cork-specific not published) and LCL per cubic metre ($60–$160/CBM), with the planning break-even near 15 CBM — below that LCL is usually cheaper, above it FCL starts to win.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What documents are needed for Irish customs clearance?',
    a: 'The core set is four documents plus one classification — commercial invoice, bill of lading (or CMR consignment note), packing list and the correct 10-digit TARIC code, backed by your EORI number. Regulated products add CE marking evidence and chemicals add REACH registration.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I defer VAT when importing into Ireland?',
    a: 'Ireland, like other EU states, allows EU customs warehousing (procedures 42/63) to defer import VAT until goods are released for free circulation — a working-capital lever worth more cash at 23% VAT than in a 19% market, so ask your broker about the procedure before assuming VAT must be paid at the quay.',
  },
];

